course: dictionary
lesson: 4115
title: Gladness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gladness is a noun, a naming word for a feeling. It means a warm, happy joy inside you. You can feel gladness, and you can show it.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «Psalm 100 calls all the earth to make a joyful noise and to worship God with gladness and thanks.» Joyful, gladness and thanks sit close together, so gladness must be a happy, thankful kind of joy.
explain: Writers use gladness to show a gentle, warm joy, the kind that fills a person quietly. Phrases like «with gladness» and «full of gladness» show how it is felt. To check your meaning, swap in joy: if the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Gladness means a feeling of being happy and joyful.
fact: Gladness is a noun, so it names a feeling. It is uncountable, so we do not say "a gladness" or "two gladnesses".
fact: Useful phrases: «with gladness», «full of gladness», and «joy and gladness».
fact: «Serve the Lord with gladness» is a line you can find in stories, poems, hymns and the Bible.
fact: In Psalm 100, gladness is joined with thanks, which shows it is a warm, grateful joy.
exercise: What does gladness mean? | *A feeling of being happy and joyful | A feeling of being lost in the dark | A loud noise made by a crowd | A feeling of being cold and tired
exercise: Find and copy one word from «make a joyful noise» that means full of joy. | make | *joyful | noise | earth
exercise: Which word could replace gladness in «worship God with gladness»? | sorrow | anger | silence | *joy
test: «Serve the Lord with gladness.» Does gladness here mean sadness, anger or joy? | Anger | *Joy | Sadness
test: Gladness is a noun. Which word is also a noun? | *Happiness | Happily | Joyfully | Happy
exam: Ella reads, «She walked into the hall full of gladness.» What does full of gladness suggest? | Very angry and loud | Very lost and afraid | Very tired and sleepy | *Very happy and joyful
